#
# Conformance case: profiles/probabilistic-marginal-independent
# AC (#506): marginals computed correctly under a DECLARED independence model.
# Two independent probabilistic facts (rain=0.5, sprinkler=0.5) feed a noisy-OR
# rule (wet :- rain; wet :- sprinkler). Under logic:FullIndependence the marginal
# of `wet` is 1 - (1-0.5)(1-0.5) = 0.75. The probabilistic facts, the model, and
# the Horn rules live in queries/wet.logic; the EDB here is only a world seed.
#
# See README.md for the full total-choice (θ) enumeration that the 0.75 golden is.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/profiles/probabilistic-marginal-independent/> .

# Schema: a sort for the projection back-ends; the inference is query-driven.
ex:Condition a logic:Kind .
